invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the conversion back from Jacobian coordinates leaves out the
  masked move, so a point at infinity whose Y is zero comes out as
  (0 : 0 : 0). That names no point, and a complete addition that reads it
  gives (0 : 0 : 0) back whatever it adds. bin/p256_equiv_test converts
  the Jacobian point with every coordinate zero, which is what
  p256_wide_mul holds for the point at infinity, and requires (0 : Y : 0)
  with Y not zero.

--- old
    o->y = a->y;
    p256_wide_fe_cmov(&o->y, &p256_wide_fe_one_mont, p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->z));
--- new
    o->y = a->y;
